<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10925" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνώγαιον</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνώγεον</span></b> , τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνω, γαῖα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything raised from the ground: the upper floor of a
				house,</i> used as a granary, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				5.4.29
			</span></i> (s.v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				312
			</span></i>; as a dining-room, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Marc.</u>
				14.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				22.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>prison,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνώγεον</span> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				1581
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Dodona</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάγαιον</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνόκαιον</span> are also found in codd., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				405
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
